"""
How text filters treat upper and lower case. It only changes startsWith,
endsWith, like and regex: equals, not, in and notIn always match case exactly,
and contains always ignores case.
"""
enum QueryMode {
    "Match case exactly (SQL LIKE and ~). Used when mode is not sent."
    default
    "Ignore case (SQL ILIKE and ~*)."
    insensitive
}

"""
Direction of a sort. Rows with no value (null) come last when ascending and
first when descending.
"""
enum SortOrder {
    "Smallest first: A to Z, oldest to newest, low to high."
    asc
    "Largest first: Z to A, newest to oldest, high to low."
    desc
}

"""
Conditions on a text value. Every condition sent must hold (they combine with
AND). A condition left out, or an empty in / notIn list, adds no filter.

In contains, startsWith and endsWith the characters % and _ are not escaped:
they still act as wildcards.

Examples:
- { equals: "John" }
- { contains: "john" }
- { in: ["active", "pending"] }
- { startsWith: "admin@", mode: insensitive }
- { isNull: true }
"""
input StringFilter {
    "Value matches this text exactly, case included. mode does not apply."
    equals: String
    "Value differs from this text, case included. Rows with no value (null) are left out too."
    not: String
    "Value is one of these, case included. An empty list adds no filter, so every row passes."
    in: [String!]
    "Value is none of these, case included. Rows with no value (null) are left out. An empty list adds no filter."
    notIn: [String!]
    "Value contains this text anywhere. Always ignores case, whatever mode says."
    contains: String
    "Value starts with this text. Case follows mode."
    startsWith: String
    "Value ends with this text. Case follows mode."
    endsWith: String
    "Raw SQL LIKE pattern: % is any run of characters, _ is one character. Case follows mode."
    like: String
    "POSIX regular expression the value must match (SQL ~). Case follows mode. An invalid pattern makes the query fail."
    regex: String
    "Case handling for startsWith, endsWith, like and regex. Case-sensitive when not sent."
    mode: QueryMode
    "true keeps only rows with no value (null); false keeps only rows with a value. An empty string counts as a value."
    isNull: Boolean
}

"""
Conditions on a whole-number value. Every condition sent must hold (they
combine with AND), so gte with lte makes a range. A condition left out, or an
empty in / notIn list, adds no filter.

Examples:
- { equals: 25 }
- { gte: 18, lte: 65 }
- { gt: 0 }
"""
input IntFilter {
    "Value equals this number."
    equals: Int
    "Value differs from this number. Rows with no value (null) are left out too."
    not: Int
    "Value is one of these numbers. An empty list adds no filter, so every row passes."
    in: [Int!]
    "Value is none of these numbers. Rows with no value (null) are left out. An empty list adds no filter."
    notIn: [Int!]
    "Value is below this number, not including it."
    lt: Int
    "Value is this number or below."
    lte: Int
    "Value is above this number, not including it."
    gt: Int
    "Value is this number or above."
    gte: Int
    "true keeps only rows with no value (null); false keeps only rows with a value."
    isNull: Boolean
}

"""
Conditions on a decimal number, such as an amount or a distance. Every
condition sent must hold (they combine with AND), so gte with lte makes a
range. A condition left out, or an empty in / notIn list, adds no filter.

Examples:
- { gte: 100.0, lte: 500.0 }
- { gt: 1000.0 }
"""
input FloatFilter {
    "Value equals this number exactly."
    equals: Float
    "Value differs from this number. Rows with no value (null) are left out too."
    not: Float
    "Value is one of these numbers. An empty list adds no filter, so every row passes."
    in: [Float!]
    "Value is none of these numbers. Rows with no value (null) are left out. An empty list adds no filter."
    notIn: [Float!]
    "Value is below this number, not including it."
    lt: Float
    "Value is this number or below."
    lte: Float
    "Value is above this number, not including it."
    gt: Float
    "Value is this number or above."
    gte: Float
    "true keeps only rows with no value (null); false keeps only rows with a value."
    isNull: Boolean
}

"""
Conditions on a yes/no value. Both conditions must hold when both are sent.
"""
input BoolFilter {
    "Value is true, or value is false. Rows with no value (null) match neither."
    equals: Boolean
    "true keeps only rows with no value (null); false keeps only rows with a value."
    isNull: Boolean
}

"""
Conditions on a date and time. Values are exact moments (see DateTime), and
moments sent with different offsets compare as the same instant. Every
condition sent must hold (they combine with AND), so gte with lt makes a
period. A condition left out, or an empty in / notIn list, adds no filter.

For one whole day, send gte at the start of the day and lt at the start of the
next day, both in the time zone that day belongs to.

Examples:
- { gte: "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z", lt: "2024-02-01T00:00:00Z" }
"""
input DateTimeFilter {
    "Value is exactly this moment. For a day or a period, use a gte / lt range instead."
    equals: DateTime
    "Value is any moment other than this one. Rows with no value (null) are left out too."
    not: DateTime
    "Value is exactly one of these moments. An empty list adds no filter, so every row passes."
    in: [DateTime!]
    "Value is none of these moments. Rows with no value (null) are left out. An empty list adds no filter."
    notIn: [DateTime!]
    "Value is before this moment, not including it."
    lt: DateTime
    "Value is at or before this moment."
    lte: DateTime
    "Value is after this moment, not including it."
    gt: DateTime
    "Value is at or after this moment."
    gte: DateTime
    "true keeps only rows with no value (null); false keeps only rows with a value."
    isNull: Boolean
}

"""
Conditions on an identifier, compared as exact text. Every condition sent must
hold (they combine with AND). A condition left out, or an empty in / notIn
list, adds no filter.
"""
input IDFilter {
    "Identifier equals this value exactly."
    equals: ID
    "Identifier differs from this value. Rows with no value (null) are left out too."
    not: ID
    "Identifier is one of these. An empty list adds no filter, so every row passes."
    in: [ID!]
    "Identifier is none of these. Rows with no value (null) are left out. An empty list adds no filter."
    notIn: [ID!]
    "true keeps only rows with no value (null); false keeps only rows with a value."
    isNull: Boolean
}

"""
Conditions on a UUID identifier. Values must be valid UUIDs; a malformed one is
rejected before the query runs. Every condition sent must hold (they combine
with AND). A condition left out, or an empty in / notIn list, adds no filter.
"""
input UUIDFilter {
    "Identifier equals this UUID."
    equals: UUID
    "Identifier differs from this UUID. Rows with no value (null) are left out too."
    not: UUID
    "Identifier is one of these UUIDs. An empty list adds no filter, so every row passes."
    in: [UUID!]
    "Identifier is none of these UUIDs. Rows with no value (null) are left out. An empty list adds no filter."
    notIn: [UUID!]
    "true keeps only rows with no value (null); false keeps only rows with a value."
    isNull: Boolean
}

"""
Conditions on a JSON value stored as PostgreSQL jsonb. Every condition sent
must hold (they combine with AND).

Known problem: hasKey, hasKeys and hasAnyKey currently build an invalid
database query, so a list call that sends any of them fails.

Examples:
- { contains: { role: "admin" } }
- { isNull: false }
"""
input JSONFilter {
    "Value is exactly this JSON: same keys and values. Key order and spacing do not matter."
    equals: JSON
    "Value contains this JSON: every key and value given is present (jsonb @>). Extra keys are fine."
    contains: JSON
    "Value holds nothing beyond this JSON: all of its keys and values appear in the one given (jsonb <@)."
    containedBy: JSON
    "Meant to keep rows whose JSON has this top-level key. Currently broken: the query fails."
    hasKey: String
    "Meant to keep rows that have all of these top-level keys. Currently broken: the query fails. An empty list adds no filter."
    hasKeys: [String!]
    "Meant to keep rows that have at least one of these top-level keys. Currently broken: the query fails. An empty list adds no filter."
    hasAnyKey: [String!]
    "true keeps only rows with no value (null); false keeps only rows with a value. A stored JSON null counts as a value."
    isNull: Boolean
}